<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 105 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 105 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 105 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>The Bank allotted the whole amount in repos to June 2.</p>
<p>It has now provided liquidity worth 315 million stg so far on Tuesday, in response to a forecast money market shortage of 1.5 billion stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
